{
  "$comment": [
    "Secret-free MCP client configuration for the refund demo.",
    "MERGE this 'refund-demo' entry into your existing client MCP config.",
    "Do NOT overwrite your config file -- you will lose your other servers.",
    "",
    "There is deliberately no token, secret, or client_id here.",
    "The client receives a 401 with a WWW-Authenticate header pointing at",
    "Protected Resource Metadata, discovers the authorization server, and runs",
    "its own OAuth flow with PKCE and an RFC 8707 resource indicator.",
    "That discovery is the thing being demonstrated -- pre-seeding a token",
    "would hide it.",
    "",
    "Resource B (http://localhost:8802/mcp) is intentionally NOT listed.",
    "It exists to prove that a token minted for it is rejected by Resource A."
  ],
  "servers": {
    "refund-demo": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://localhost:8801/mcp"
    }
  }
}
